## Project-based security

~> The `security` block may need the [Matrix Authorization Strategy Plugin](https://plugins.jenkins.io/matrix-auth/) installed and enabled in the system's Global Security settings in order to function properly.

~> `permissions` was a list before **v1.2.2** and is a set from v1.2.2 onward. Existing `permissions = [...]` configuration keeps working unchanged, but expressions that index into the attribute do not — see [Upgrading to v1.2.2](../guides/upgrading-to-1.2.2).

Each entry pairs a Jenkins permission with the user or group it is granted to:

```hcl
security {
  permissions = [
    "hudson.model.Item.Build:username",
    "hudson.model.Item.Cancel:username",
    "hudson.model.Item.Configure:username",
    "hudson.model.Item.Create:username",
    "hudson.model.Item.Delete:username",
  ]
}
```

## Kubernetes Cloud access

Set `permitted_kubernetes_clouds` to the names of existing Clouds with **Restrict pipeline support to authorized folders** enabled. The [Kubernetes plugin](https://plugins.jenkins.io/kubernetes/#restricting-what-jobs-can-use-your-configured-cloud) grants those Clouds to pipelines in this folder and its descendants.

```hcl
resource "jenkins_folder" "team" {
  name                        = "platform-team"
  permitted_kubernetes_clouds = ["platform-agents"]
}
```

Omit the attribute to preserve the folder's direct grants. Use `[]` to remove them. Parent grants are inherited independently of this attribute.

## Pipeline libraries

~> `pipeline_libraries` needs the [Pipeline: Groovy Libraries Plugin](https://plugins.jenkins.io/pipeline-groovy-lib/) and the [Git Plugin](https://plugins.jenkins.io/git/) installed.

Set `pipeline_libraries` to the [folder-level Pipeline libraries](https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/pipeline/shared-libraries/#folder-level-shared-libraries) pipelines in this folder and its descendants may load. Each library is retrieved from a Git repository through a Git SCM source that discovers branches. Folder-level libraries run in the Groovy sandbox.

```hcl
resource "jenkins_folder" "team" {
  name = "platform-team"

  pipeline_libraries = [
    {
      name               = "team-steps"
      default_version    = "main"
      git_remote         = "https://git.example.com/platform/team-steps.git"
      git_credentials_id = "git-token"
    },
  ]
}
```

Omit the attribute to leave the folder's libraries unmanaged: Terraform neither reads nor changes them, and removing the attribute from a configuration leaves the libraries on the folder. Use `[]` to remove them. A configured list replaces every library on the folder, including one with a retriever other than a Git SCM source, which is reported with a null `git_remote`.
